Indonesian Marines are pouring into the  area devastated by an earthquake and  tsunami to help with rescues the death  toll climbed overnight to more than 1420  and janeshia still has not evacuated all  of the injured six days after the  disasters Ben Tracy is in hard-hit  helloo with the growing sense of despair  nearly 70,000 people here are now  homeless there's no drinking water  there's no electricity there's nowhere  to buy food and for six days now people  have been waiting for help to arrive the  Indonesian military is finally here with  an army of supplies boxes of water  instant noodles and giant sacks full of  clothes all of it is desperately needed  at the many makeshift homeless camps  that have sprung up all over the  disaster zone this woman named n dong  has been here with her one-year-old  daughter Wuhan for six days a tent is  their only protection from ninety degree  heat they have had a drink water from  the nearby river which is also being  used as a toilet  do you have any idea of how long you'll  be here she says I don't know where to  go I no longer have a home her home was  wiped out by the tsunami triggered by  the 7.5 magnitude earthquake last Friday  the scars on Wu Hans face are from being  rolled by the tsunami waves she says it  is a miracle we found her alive I thank  God she has a new life while we were at  the homeless camp we also saw this man  walking around wearing a sign it  basically says I'm looking for my wife  and I'm looking for my son and he just  told me that he has not seen either of  them since the earthquake happened six  days ago he's holding out hope that they  may still be alive but this is what his  neighborhood now looks like every single  home reduced to piles of charred debris  and we're told that more than 700 homes  were destroyed here during the  earthquake there is now so much debris  here and so little to move it with that  it's hard to imagine how long it's going  to take for them to try to find all the  people who are likely buried here sadly  they expect to find many more  victims this city holds a mass burial  everyday and just dug in second mass  grave for CBS this morning Ben Tracy  Pulu Indonesia Ben Tracy thanks that  cardboard sign just breaks your heart  well mass graves - I mean the numbers  are staggering - are the numbers
 

